<section class="c-hero"><div class="c-container c-hero__inner"><div><h1>Design your home using civica styles, components and patterns</h1><p>Make Home Assistant clear, consistent and easier to use. Start with established public service design, adapted for the devices, information and everyday tasks in your home.</p><a class="c-start-button" href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/index.html') %>">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">❯</span></a></div><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/design-system-hero.svg') %>" alt="" width="420" height="350"></div></section>
<div class="c-container c-home-sections">
<section class="c-project-intro c-home-section" aria-labelledby="project-purpose"><h2 id="project-purpose">Why I created civica</h2><p>I created civica to make everyday Home Assistant controls clearer for the whole household, including older relatives, neurodivergent people and guests. This independent project adapts the GOV.UK Design System’s research and reusable patterns into predictable layouts, readable text and clear actions. It is not affiliated with GOV.UK or the UK government.</p><p><a href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/about.html') %>">Read about the project and why I created it</a></p></section>
<section class="c-whats-new c-home-section c-home-columns" aria-labelledby="whats-new"><div><h2 id="whats-new">What’s new</h2><h3><span class="govuk-caption-m">13 November 2026</span>A simpler name: civica</h3><p>The project is now called civica, with revised house-symbol artwork and a shorter repository address. The <a href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/install.html') %>">installation guide</a> explains the default civica theme, current release files and how to update an existing installation.</p><h3>12 November 2026: Home Assistant coverage and writing guidance</h3><p>Explore <a href="<%= docs_path('/home-assistant/index.html') %>">38 Home Assistant specifications</a> for device controls and household tasks. The <a href="<%= docs_path('/content/index.html') %>">Writing guide</a> now has its own section, with plain English guidance and a dated Home Assistant terminology reference.</p><p><a href="<%= docs_path('/community/home-assistant-coverage-audit.html') %>">Read the coverage and verification record</a></p></div><div><h3>Follow the project</h3><p>See the theme features that have been agreed, are being worked on or have been delivered.</p><p><a href="<%= docs_path('/community/roadmap.html') %>">Explore the theme roadmap</a></p><p><a href="https://github.com/nathcymru/civica/releases">View releases on GitHub</a></p></div></section>
<section class="c-home-categories c-home-section" aria-label="Explore the design system">
<article class="c-home-card" aria-labelledby="styles-title"><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/category-styles.svg') %>" alt="" width="320" height="140"><div class="c-home-card__body"><h2 id="styles-title"><a href="<%= docs_path('/styles/index.html') %>">Styles</a></h2><p>Create a clear, consistent interface with guidance on colour, typography, spacing and images.</p></div></article>
<article class="c-home-card" aria-labelledby="components-title"><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/category-components.svg') %>" alt="" width="320" height="140"><div class="c-home-card__body"><h2 id="components-title"><a href="<%= docs_path('/components/index.html') %>">Components</a></h2><p>Build your interface with reusable buttons, forms, device cards and charts.</p></div></article>
<article class="c-home-card" aria-labelledby="patterns-title"><img src="<%= docs_path('/images/category-patterns.svg') %>" alt="" width="320" height="140"><div class="c-home-card__body"><h2 id="patterns-title"><a href="<%= docs_path('/patterns/index.html') %>">Patterns</a></h2><p>Help people complete everyday tasks with layouts for rooms, controls and household information.</p></div></article>
</section>
<section class="c-home-band c-home-section c-home-columns" aria-label="Using the design system"><div><h2>Writing guide</h2><p>Use plain English to explain what the home is doing, what someone can change and what happens next. Find guidance for labels, instructions, alerts and Home Assistant terminology.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/content/index.html') %>">Write for a connected home</a></div><div><h2>Know what is implemented</h2><p>A reference example describes a design. A theme changes appearance. The optional companion adds specific interactions. Each has a different scope.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/get-started/compatibility.html') %>">Check compatibility and limits</a></div></section>
<section class="c-home-columns c-home-support c-home-section" aria-label="Accessibility and community"><div><h2>Design for everyone</h2><p>Build around readable content, keyboard access, clear focus, useful labels and alternatives to visual information.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/accessibility/index.html') %>">Accessibility principles and checks</a></div><div><h2>Help improve the system</h2><p>Share evidence from real household tasks. Document differences, test examples and keep guidance connected to the implementation.</p><a href="<%= docs_path('/community/index.html') %>">Contribute to civica</a></div></section>
</div>
